  "result": "The fix is planned but not applied. Plan mode is on, and `ExitPlanMode` isn't available in this session, so I can't submit the plan for approval.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` (line 623) uses `shlex.shlex(string, posix=True)`. By default, shlex treats `#` as a comment start, so everything from the `#` onward is dropped from the split arguments.\n\n**Planned fix:**\n- Set `lex.commenters = \"\"` right after creating the lexer, so `#` is an ordinary character.\n- Add tests in `tests/test_shell_completion.py`, e.g. `split_arg_string(\"a b#c d\") == [\"a\", \"b#c\", \"d\"]`, plus a completion case with `#` in an earlier argument.\n- Add a note to `CHANGES.md`.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-crystalline-liskov.md`. Tell me to proceed and I'll make the edits and run `pytest tests/test_shell_completion.py tests/test_parser.py`.",
